# PART 15 — DASHBOARD AND REPORTING ACCURACY

All dashboards must derive values from normalized database records.

Correct the legacy workbook's known problems:

## Forex Formula Problem

Do not use:

Received INR − Full FOB INR

as realized forex for partially paid invoices.

Calculate forex at payment-allocation level.

## Outstanding Invoice Problem

Do not determine unpaid status merely by checking whether Received INR is blank.

Use actual invoice USD minus allocated USD.

## Bank Charges Problem

Do not automatically classify every small USD shortfall as bank charges.

Only use verified recorded charges.

## BRC Deadline Problem

Do not extract statutory deadlines exclusively from remarks.

Use structured dates and configurable approved rules.

## Incentive Status Problem

Do not treat blank status cells as confirmed pending claims.

Use explicit statuses and reconciliation.

All dashboard totals must reconcile with underlying records.

